SUMMARY:W01 • Prep — DC Lab Kit Check
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN
  THESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.i
 o/alfred-university/week.html?week=1\n• Search this topic: https://num
 berclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Electricity%20Basics%
 20%2B%20Safety%20%2B%20Ohm/Watt\n• Lab Center: https://numberclaw2.git
 hub.io/alfred-university/labs.html\n• Assessment Center: https://numbe
 rclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/assessments.html\n• Engineering Lib
 rary: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCA
 REER CONNECTION: Foundational circuit measurement and safe troubleshooti
 ng.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complet
 e the required work first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\n
 \nTODAY — ACTION CHECKLIST:\n1. Open LAB-001 in Practice → Lab Cente
 r → Week 01.\n2. Choose your route. Virtual route: web browser only. P
 hysical route: low-voltage bench supply or battery (power source)\; DMM 
 (measure voltage/current/resistance)\; breadboard (solderless assembly)\
 ; LED (load)\; 220 Ω\, 330 Ω\, or 1 kΩ 1/4-watt resistor (current lim
 iting)\; jumper wires (connections).\n3. Physical check: inspect leads a
 nd wires\, confirm the DMM fuse/leads are intact\, identify LED polarity
 \, and keep power disconnected while building.\n4. If physical equipment
  is missing\, use the approved Falstad virtual route instead of stopping
  the course.\n5. The prep reminder is complete when you have confirmed o
 ne workable route for LAB-001.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n
 • Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Googl
 e Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6
 th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nAFTER TOD
 AY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES\nBy the end of this event\, you should
  be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Know what equipment/parts are r
 equired for the next practical session and what each item is for.\n• C
 onfirm every critical item is ready\, compatible\, and safe to use befor
 e the lab begins.\n• Identify any missing item early enough to obtain 
 or substitute it without cancelling the hands-on work.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT
 \nThe assigned resources and tasks above are intended to cover every ite
 m in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one o
 f these items after the session\, do not count that item as complete. Wr
 ite the concept on a short catch-up list and use the linked official or 
 supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\
 nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If y
 ou cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on 
 a short catch-up list and repair it during the next available review blo
 ck. No spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Equipment\,Embedded\,CETa
END:VEVENT
