SUMMARY:W01 • Learn — Electricity\, Safety & Ohm’s Law
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN
  THESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.i
 o/alfred-university/week.html?week=1\n• Search this topic: https://num
 berclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Electricity%20Basics%
 20%2B%20Safety%20%2B%20Ohm/Watt\n• Engineering Library: https://number
 claw2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Fou
 ndational circuit measurement and safe troubleshooting.\nRESOURCE PRIORI
 TY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work 
 first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nSTART FROM ZERO — 
 SESSION 1\nWHY THIS STARTS HERE: Every later embedded-system skill assum
 es you understand what voltage\, current\, resistance\, power\, ground\,
  polarity\, open circuits\, shorts\, and safe measurement mean. We are n
 ot assuming prior electronics knowledge.\n\nWEEK 1 FOCUS: START FROM ZER
 O: Safety + What Electricity Is + Voltage / Current / Resistance + Ohm /
  Watt + SI Prefixes\nETA/CETa SCOPE — FIRST PASS: 1.1\, 1.4–1.7\, 1.
 10\, 1.13–1.14\; 2.1\, 2.4\, 2.6\, 2.13–2.14\; 9.8–9.9. The narrow
 er RF/fiber/field-safety details return later in CETa-specific review.\n
 CAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Build the vocabulary and safety habits every la
 ter circuit\, instrument\, microcontroller\, and troubleshooting skill d
 epends on. Set up the Git evidence notebook from day one.\n\nTODAY — 8
 :00 PM TO 9:30 PM:\n1. Safety first (10 min): electrical shock basics\, 
 de-energizing\, ESD\, and why resistance measurements are made on de-ene
 rgized circuits.\n2. What electricity is (15 min): charge/electrons at a
  practical technician level\; do not get buried in atomic physics.\n3. L
 earn voltage vs current vs resistance vs power (25 min). Explain each in
  your own words before moving on.\n4. Open the ETA Common Formulas sheet
  and locate Ohm's law / power relationships (5 min).\n5. Work 6–8 begi
 nner Ohm/Watt problems with units (15 min). Show the rearrangement\; do 
 not copy an example.\n6. Set up or confirm the GitHub lab notebook/repos
 itory (10 min). Create a Week_01 folder/note.\n\nMASTERY GATE: In plain 
 language\, explain charge\, voltage\, current\, resistance\, power\, pol
 arity\, open vs short\, and basic ESD/shock precautions\; use SI prefixe
 s\; solve fresh Ohm/Watt problems\; then build and safely measure a curr
 ent-limited LED circuit on Saturday.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Learn from the bot
 tom. Watching alone never counts. Use learn → retrieve → calculate/c
 ode → build/measure → debug → document. Start later study blocks w
 ith ~10 minutes of spaced recall. A missed session never creates an unhe
 althy make-up marathon.\n\nWEEK 1 START-FROM-ZERO RESOURCES:\n• Electr
 ic Current and Circuits Explained: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r-SCy
 D7f_zI\n• Electrical Safety Training: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=
 TMT6f3tZQSk\n• GitHub Skills — Introduction to GitHub: https://githu
 b.com/skills/introduction-to-github\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINK
 S:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/G
 oogle Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• E
 TA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFIC
 IAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.1 pp.1–6 SKIM o
 nly\; Ch.2 pp.7–14\; Ch.3 pp.16–18\; Ch.4 pp.25–26\; read the book
  addendum once.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.2 quiz p.15 after the safety lesson. 
 Use answers p.223 only after finishing.\nWHY: Starts from zero with safe
 ty\, units\, Ohm/Watt and the physical meaning of voltage/current/resist
 ance before circuit analysis.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the 
 primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA erra
 ta control whenever the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\n
 AFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 01)\nBy the end of this
  event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Explain volt
 age\, current\, resistance\, power\, ground/reference\, polarity\, open 
 circuits\, and short circuits.\n• Use SI prefixes and engineering nota
 tion correctly for common electronic values.\n• Apply Ohm's law and th
 e Watt/power relationships to simple DC circuits.\n• Recognize basic e
 lectrical hazards and use safe low-voltage measurement habits.\n\nCOVERA
 GE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are intended to cover e
 very item in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstra
 te one of these items after the session\, do not count that item as comp
 lete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use the linked offi
 cial or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETI
 ON RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learning outcomes bel
 ow. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one con
 cept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next available re
 view block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT30M
