 tps://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CON
 NECTION: Foundational circuit measurement and safe troubleshooting.\nRES
 OURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the re
 quired work first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nNeed by 
 Week 3. Confirm bench supply\, oscilloscope\, appropriate probes/leads\,
  safe low-voltage source/circuit\, and any adapters. If you do not own a
 n instrument yet\, record the acquisition plan\; do not improvise unsafe
  measurements.\n\n\nTODAY — ACTION CHECKLIST:\n1. Open LAB-003 in Prac
 tice → Lab Center → Week 03.\n2. Virtual route: web browser plus Fal
 stad and the Tektronix virtual-oscilloscope resource linked in LAB-003.\
 n3. Physical route: DMM with leads\; adjustable low-voltage bench supply
  with output leads\; oscilloscope\; a compatible 1×/10× probe and grou
 nd lead\; breadboard/test circuit\; function generator only if available
 .\n4. Confirm the probe is not damaged\, the scope and probe ratings exc
 eed the planned low-voltage signal\, and the supply starts at zero/curre
 nt-limited where supported.\n5. If an instrument is missing\, use the co
 mplete virtual route. Do not improvise measurements on mains voltage.\n\
 nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study G
 uide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page 
 numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.or
 g/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES\
 nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate
 :\n• Know what equipment/parts are required for the next practical ses
 sion and what each item is for.\n• Confirm every critical item is read
 y\, compatible\, and safe to use before the lab begins.\n• Identify an
 y missing item early enough to obtain or substitute it without cancellin
 g the hands-on work.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks
  above are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you sti
 ll cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, 
 do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-u
 p list and use the linked official or supplemental resource before closi
 ng the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then c
 heck the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate a
 n outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair i
 t during the next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is requ
 ired.
