SUMMARY:W02 • Learn — DC Circuits\, KVL/KCL & Voltage Dividers
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN
  THESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.i
 o/alfred-university/week.html?week=2\n• Search this topic: https://num
 berclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=DC%20Networks%20%2B%2
 0KVL/KCL%20%2B%20Voltage%20Dividers%20%2B%20DMM\n• Engineering Library
 : https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER
  CONNECTION: Foundational circuit measurement and safe troubleshooting.\
 nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete th
 e required work first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK
  2 FOCUS: DC Networks + KVL/KCL + Voltage Dividers + DMM\nETA/CETa SCOPE
 : 4.1\; 4.10\; 4.17\; 3.1.4\; 8.1–8.4\; 8.16\; 9.1–9.2\nCAREER/EMBED
 DED PURPOSE: Series/parallel networks\, voltage/current division\, meter
  range/connection\, LTspice prediction vs measurement.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RE
 SOURCES:\n- Electronic Circuits playlist: https://www.youtube.com/playli
 st?list=PL0o_zxa4K1BV9E-N8tSExU1djL6slnjbL\n- ETA Common Formulas: https
 ://www.etai.org/Common_Formulas.pdf\n- LTspice: https://www.analog.com/e
 n/resources/design-tools-and-calculators/ltspice-simulator.html\n\nMASTE
 RY GATE: Solve unseen series/parallel/KVL/KCLproblems\, predict test poi
 nts\, then verify a built divider network with DMM and explain any measu
 rement error.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: watching alone never counts. Use learn ->
  retrieve -> calculate/code ->build/measure -> debug -> document. Start 
 each non-exam study block with~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never use a 
 missed session as justification for an unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTO
 DAY:\nStudy only the resources tied to this week’s competencies. Creat
 e a one-page summary and 5–10 recall prompts. First 10 min: spaced ret
 rieval from older material.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• 
 Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Dr
 ive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-e
 d. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUD
 Y GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.3 p.19 series/parallel fo
 rmulas + Ch.4 pp.27–34.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.4 quiz p.34\, then Unit 2 r
 eview p.35.\nWHY: The book's DC-circuit sequence aligns directly with se
 ries/parallel\, KVL/KCL\, voltage dividers and troubleshooting.\nSOURCE 
 RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA com
 petency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older book dif
 fers or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTC
 OMES (WEEK 02)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain
  or demonstrate:\n• Analyze series and parallel resistor networks.\n
 • Use Kirchhoff's Voltage Law and Kirchhoff's Current Law to reason ab
 out circuit behavior.\n• Design and analyze a voltage divider\, includ
 ing the effect of loading.\n• Predict node voltages\, branch currents\
 , equivalent resistance\, and power.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned res
 ources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outcome 
 list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items afte
 r the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on
  a short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental resou
 rce before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assign
 ed work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain 
 or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up l
 ist and repair it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet
  logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
