 /C/L Behavior + Frequency/Period/RMS\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 2.8–2.12.2\; 4.2
 –4.4\; 9.3\; 9.7\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: RC timing\, decoupling\, in
 ductive behavior\, waveform reading\; relate frequency-domain concepts t
 o embedded signals.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- Capacitors and Inductor
 s playlist: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLB9A78ED3D7EF1AE5\n-E
 TA Common Formulas: https://www.etai.org/Common_Formulas.pdf\n-Electroni
 c Circuits playlist: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL0o_zxa4K1BV
 9E-N8tSExU1djL6slnjbL\n\nMASTERY GATE: Convert frequency/period\, identi
 fy peak/peak-to-peak/RMS\, explain phase qualitatively\, calculate RCtim
 ing\, and capture an RC waveform.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alonenever c
 ounts. Use learn -> retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure-> debug 
 -> document. Start each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced 
 recall. Never use a missed session as justification for anunhealthy make
 -up marathon.\n\nTODAY — ACTION CHECKLIST:\n1. Open LAB-004 — RC Tim
 e Constant + Filter Response in Practice → Lab Center → Week 04.\n2.
  Choose one route. Virtual needs: Web browser only. Physical needs: Osci
 lloscope\, function generator\, breadboard\, R/C components.\n3. Follow 
 every numbered step under the route you selected\; predict the result be
 fore simulating\, building\, or measuring.\n4. Save the required evidenc
 e: Calculations + two simulator scope captures + short interpretation.\n
 5. Mark only the route you actually completed. A virtual completion does
  not claim physical bench experience.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LI
 NKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned
 /Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n•
  ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFF
 ICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.3 pp.19–24 + 
 Ch.6 pp.45–46.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Fresh problems from the assigned pages\
 ; no answer-key checking until you have committed answers.\nWHY: Builds 
 AC waveform\, RMS\, frequency/period\, capacitance\, inductance and firs
 t-order reactive behavior.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the pri
 mary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata 
 control whenever the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFT
 ER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 04)\nBy the end of this ev
 ent\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Describe sine w
 aves and basic AC quantities: amplitude\, peak\, peak-to-peak\, frequenc
 y\, period\, phase\, and RMS.\n• Convert between frequency and period 
 and interpret waveform measurements.\n• Explain how capacitors and ind
 uctors store energy and oppose changes in voltage or current.\n• Descr
 ibe RC and RL transient behavior and the idea of a time constant.\n• C
 alculate frequency/period\, RMS or peak relationships where assigned\, a
 nd basic RC timing quantities.\n• Read waveform scales accurately and 
 connect numerical results to scope displays.\n• Recognize basic low-pa
 ss and high-pass behavior.\n• Use an oscilloscope to connect waveform 
 theory to measured circuit behavior.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned res
 ources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outcome 
 list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items afte
 r the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on
  a short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental resou
 rce before closing the gap.\n\nWEEK-END MASTERY RULE\nThis practical is 
 the cumulative proof point for the week. The week is Green only when the
  knowledge can be used on real hardware/code/measurements without follow
 ing a step-by-step tutorial.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assig
 ned work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain
  or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up 
 list and repair it during the next available review block. No spreadshee
 t logging is required.
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
