  OUTCOMES (WEEK 06)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to ex
 plain or demonstrate:\n• Explain capacitive reactance\, inductive reac
 tance\, impedance\, and their dependence on frequency.\n• Recognize th
 e relationship among resistance\, reactance\, impedance\, voltage\, curr
 ent\, and phase.\n• Explain resonance and the role of inductance and c
 apacitance in tuned behavior.\n• Describe basic low-pass\, high-pass\,
  band-pass\, and band-stop filter behavior.\n• Calculate basic XL\, XC
 \, impedance/ratio/resonance relationships at the assigned CETa depth.\n
 • Predict how changing frequency changes circuit behavior.\n• Explai
 n transformer turns ratio\, voltage/current relationships\, isolation\, 
 and basic loading ideas.\n• Use calculations\, simulation\, or measure
 ments to verify frequency-dependent circuit behavior.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\
 nThe assigned resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item
  in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of
  these items after the session\, do not count that item as complete. Wri
 te the concept on a short catch-up list and use the linked official or s
 upplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nWEEK-END MASTERY RULE\nT
 his practical is the cumulative proof point for the week. The week is Gr
 een only when the knowledge can be used on real hardware/code/measuremen
 ts without following a step-by-step tutorial.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\
 nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If y
 ou cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on 
