 20Switching%20Devices\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.gith
 ub.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Component-lev
 el analog/digital troubleshooting and instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORIT
 Y: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work f
 irst\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 8 FOCUS: Semicon
 ductors: Diodes + BJT/FET/MOSFET + SCR/TRIAC\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 3.5–3.7.
 3\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Switching\, biasing\, logic-level MOSFETs\, 
 flyback diodes\, Zener regulation\, semiconductor fault symptoms.\n\nTHI
 S WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n-Electronics for Beginners: https://www.youtube.com
 /playlist?list=PLzqS33DOPhJkRn6e9_OTdQwRojO8qlusI\n- NMOS vs PMOS / Enha
 ncement vs Depletion: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kY-ka0PriaE\n- ETA
  CETa competencies: https://www.etai.org/comps/CETa_comps.pdf\n\nMASTERY
  GATE: identify devices and terminals\, analyze simple bias/current/powe
 r\, select a transistor/MOSFET as a switch\, and troubleshoot one intent
 ionally miswired circuit.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts. 
 Use learn -> retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug ->docu
 ment. Start each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall.
  Never use a missed session as justification for an unhealthy make-up ma
 rathon.\n\nTODAY:\nStudy only the resources tied to THIS WEEK’s compet
 encies. Create a one-page summary and 5–10 recall prompts. First 10 mi
 n: spaced retrieval from older material.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE
  LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scan
 ned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n
 • ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\n
 OFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.9 pp.70–78
  + Ch.10 pp.79–83.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.9 quiz p.78\, Ch.10 quiz p.83 an
 d Unit 4 review p.84.\nWHY: Directly supports semiconductor recognition\
 , switching behavior and discrete-device troubleshooting.\nSOURCE RULE: 
 The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competenc
 y wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older book differs o
 r omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (
 WEEK 08)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain or de
 monstrate:\n• Explain PN junction behavior and the operation/use of re
 ctifier diodes\, LEDs\, Zener diodes\, and protection diodes.\n• Expla
 in BJT switching at a practical level and distinguish NPN/PNP behavior.\
 n• Explain FET/MOSFET gate control\, source/drain roles\, logic-level 
 switching\, and common protection concerns.\n• Recognize SCR/TRIAC pur
 pose and where controlled switching devices are used.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\
 nThe assigned resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item
  in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of
  these items after the session\, do not count that item as complete. Wri
 te the concept on a short catch-up list and use the linked official or s
 upplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\n
 Finish the assigned work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If yo
 u cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a
  short catch-up list and repair it during the next available review bloc
 k. No spreadsheet logging is required.
END:VALARM
