 level analog/digital troubleshooting and instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIO
 RITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required wor
 k first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 8 FOCUS: Semi
 conductors: Diodes + BJT/FET/MOSFET + SCR/TRIAC\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 3.5–3
 .7.3\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Switching\, biasing\, logic-level MOSFETs
 \, flyback diodes\, Zener regulation\, semiconductor fault symptoms.\n\n
 THIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n-Electronics for Beginners: https://www.youtube.
 com/playlist?list=PLzqS33DOPhJkRn6e9_OTdQwRojO8qlusI\n- NMOS vs PMOS / E
 nhancement vs Depletion: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kY-ka0PriaE\n- 
 ETA CETa competencies: https://www.etai.org/comps/CETa_comps.pdf\n\nMAST
 ERY GATE: identify devices and terminals\, analyze simple bias/current/p
 ower\, select a transistor/MOSFET as a switch\, and troubleshoot one int
 entionally miswired circuit.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never count
 s. Use learn -> retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug ->d
 ocument. Start each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced reca
 ll. Never use a missed session as justification for an unhealthy make-up
  marathon.\n\nTODAY — ACTION CHECKLIST:\n1. Open LAB-008 — Diode / B
 JT / MOSFET Switching in Practice → Lab Center → Week 08.\n2. Choose
  one route. Virtual needs: Web browser only. Physical needs: DMM diode m
 ode\, LEDs/diodes\, BJT\, logic MOSFET\, resistors\, supply.\n3. Follow 
 every numbered step under the route you selected\; predict the result be
 fore simulating\, building\, or measuring.\n4. Save the required evidenc
 e: Device observations + BJT/MOSFET switch screenshots + fault note.\n5.
  Mark only the route you actually completed. A virtual completion does n
 ot claim physical bench experience.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINK
 S:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/G
 oogle Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• E
 TA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFIC
 IAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.9 pp.70–78 + Ch
 .10 pp.79–83.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.9 quiz p.78\, Ch.10 quiz p.83 and Uni
 t 4 review p.84.\nWHY: Directly supports semiconductor recognition\, swi
 tching behavior and discrete-device troubleshooting.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6
 th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wor
 ding + current ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or omi
 ts a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 
 08)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain or demonst
 rate:\n• Explain PN junction behavior and the operation/use of rectifi
 er diodes\, LEDs\, Zener diodes\, and protection diodes.\n• Explain BJ
 T switching at a practical level and distinguish NPN/PNP behavior.\n• 
 Explain FET/MOSFET gate control\, source/drain roles\, logic-level switc
 hing\, and common protection concerns.\n• Recognize SCR/TRIAC purpose 
 and where controlled switching devices are used.\n• Reason about diode
  drops\, current limiting\, transistor/MOSFET switching conditions\, and
  device ratings.\n• Recognize whether a semiconductor device is being 
 used safely within its stated limits.\n• Select and wire a basic trans
 istor/MOSFET switch with appropriate current limiting/flyback protection
 .\n• Troubleshoot common semiconductor-switching faults with a meter o
 r scope.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are i
 ntended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot ex
 plain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not count
  that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and u
 se the linked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\
 n\nWEEK-END MASTERY RULE\nThis practical is the cumulative proof point f
 or the week. The week is Green only when the knowledge can be used on re
 al hardware/code/measurements without following a step-by-step tutorial.
 \n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the le
 arning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\,
  write that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during th
 e next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
