DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN
  THESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.i
 o/alfred-university/week.html?week=9\n• Search this topic: https://num
 berclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Electronic%20Power%20
 Supplies\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-
 university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Component-level analog/dig
 ital troubleshooting and instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core 
 → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use De
 ep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 9 FOCUS: Power Supplies + Rec
 tifiers + Regulation + Protection\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 10.1–10.11\; 1.4\nC
 AREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Power trees\, linear vs switching supply\, recti
 fication/filtering/regulation\, fuse/protection placement\, 3.3V/5 V rai
 l awareness.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- Linear Power Supply: https://w
 ww.youtube.com/watch?v=UTetQhGyUVg\n- Switch-Mode Power Supply: https://
 www.youtube.com/watch?v=3FyXqNcqvRM\n- ETA Common Formulas: https://www.
 etai.org/Common_Formulas.pdf\n\nMASTERY GATE: Trace asupply block diagra
 m\, calculate expected DC outputs\, identify rectifier/filter/regulator 
 stages\, and isolate one likely supplyfault.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching a
 lone never counts. Use learn ->retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measu
 re -> debug -> document. start each non-exam study block with ~10 minute
 s of spaced recall. Never use a missed session as justification for an u
 nhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nStudy only the resources tied to t
 his week’s competencies. Create a one-page summary and 5–10 recall p
 rompts. first 10 min: spaced retrieval from older material.\n\nREFERENCE
  HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th
  ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in
  BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdAST
 ErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / U
 SE: Ch.11 pp.85–90.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.11 quiz p.90.\nWHY: The entire 
 chapter maps cleanly to power-supply architecture\, rectification\, filt
 ering\, regulation and faults.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the
  primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA err
 ata control whenever the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\
 nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 09)\nBy the end of thi
 s event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Describe th
 e functional blocks of an electronic power supply: transformation/conver
 sion\, rectification\, filtering\, regulation\, and protection.\n• Exp
 lain half-wave/full-wave/bridge rectification and the purpose of filter 
 capacitors.\n• Distinguish basic linear regulation from switching regu
 lation.\n• Explain ripple\, load regulation\, line regulation\, effici
 ency\, and current limiting at a practical level.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe
  assigned resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in 
 this outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of the
 se items after the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write t
 he concept on a short catch-up list and use the linked official or suppl
 emental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFini
 sh the assigned work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you ca
 nnot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a sho
 rt catch-up list and repair it during the next available review block. N
 o spreadsheet logging is required.
