 B%20Number%20Systems\n• Assessment Center: https://numberclaw2.github.
 io/alfred-university/assessments.html\n• Engineering Library: https://
 numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTIO
 N: Component-level analog/digital troubleshooting and instrumentation.\n
 RESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the
  required work first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 
 11 FOCUS: Digital Logic + Number Systems + Boolean + Logic Families\nETA
 /CETa SCOPE: 13.1–13.12\; 9.4–9.5\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Binary/h
 ex\, truth tables\, TTL/CMOS levels\, flip-flops\, counters\, clocks\, b
 uses\, pull-ups/pull-downs and floating inputs.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES
 :\n- Digital Electronics — ALL ABOUT ELECTRONICS: https://www.youtube.
 com/playlist?list=PLwjK_iyK4LLBC_so3odA64E2MLgIRKafl\n- Digital Electron
 ics — Neso Academy: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLBlnK6fEyqR
 jMH3mWf6kwqiTbT798eAOm\n\nMASTERY GATE: Convert number systems\, build t
 ruth tables\, explain TTL/CMOS levels and sequential devices\, and diagn
 ose a floating-input/logic-state fault.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone 
 nevercounts. Use learn -> retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure ->
 debug -> document. Start each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes ofsp
 aced recall. Never use a missed session as justification for anunhealthy
  make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nApply the concept in LTspice\, C\, STM32\,
  schematic analysis or bench planning as appropriate. Predict results be
 fore simulation/code execution\; deliberately create one faultwhen safe.
 \n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Stud
 y Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED pa
 ge numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai
 .org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNM
 ENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.16 pp.132–143.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Hold the full Ch.16
  quiz until W14 after computer-basics pages are finished.\nWHY: Covers n
 umber systems\, logic families\, gates\, Boolean logic and sequential ci
 rcuits before MCU work.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primar
 y CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata con
 trol whenever the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER 
 TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 11)\nBy the end of this event
 \, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Distinguish combin
 ational from sequential logic and recognize latches/flip-flops/counters 
 at a basic level.\n• Explain logic-high/logic-low levels\, noise margi
 ns\, pull-ups/pull-downs\, floating inputs\, and open-drain/open-collect
 or concepts.\n• Recognize memory\, buses\, ports\, and basic digital-s
 ystem blocks.\n• Verify digital behavior using truth tables\, simulati
 on\, or measured logic signals.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resource
 s and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outcome list.
  If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the
  session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a sh
 ort catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental resource b
 efore closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned wo
 rk\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or de
 monstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list a
 nd repair it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet logg
 ing is required.
