 T798eAOm\n\nMASTERY GATE: Convert number systems\, build truth tables\, 
 explain TTL/CMOS levels and sequential devices\, and diagnose a floating
 -input/logic-state fault.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone nevercounts. U
 se learn -> retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure ->debug -> docum
 ent. Start each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes ofspaced recall. N
 ever use a missed session as justification for anunhealthy make-up marat
 hon.\n\nTODAY — ACTION CHECKLIST:\n1. Open LAB-011 — Digital Logic /
  Pull Resistors / Debounce in Practice → Lab Center → Week 11.\n2. C
 hoose one route. Virtual needs: Web browser only. Physical needs: Logic 
 ICs or MCU board\, switches\, resistors\, logic analyzer/scope.\n3. Foll
 ow every numbered step under the route you selected\; predict the result
  before simulating\, building\, or measuring.\n4. Save the required evid
 ence: Truth table + logic-level evidence + analyzer/simulator capture + 
 debounce note.\n5. Mark only the route you actually completed. A virtual
  completion does not claim physical bench experience.\n\nREFERENCE HUB 
 — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.:
  use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK
  ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrat
 aSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: C
 h.16 pp.132–143.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Hold the full Ch.16 quiz until W14 af
 ter computer-basics pages are finished.\nWHY: Covers number systems\, lo
 gic families\, gates\, Boolean logic and sequential circuits before MCU 
 work.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. C
 urrent ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the 
 older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED
  LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 11)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be a
 ble to explain or demonstrate:\n• Convert among binary\, decimal\, and
  hexadecimal and use binary place value confidently.\n• Explain Boolea
 n logic and the behavior/truth tables of NOT\, AND\, OR\, NAND\, NOR\, X
 OR\, and XNOR.\n• Distinguish combinational from sequential logic and 
 recognize latches/flip-flops/counters at a basic level.\n• Explain log
 ic-high/logic-low levels\, noise margins\, pull-ups/pull-downs\, floatin
 g inputs\, and open-drain/open-collector concepts.\n• Convert binary/d
 ecimal/hex\, complete truth tables\, and evaluate Boolean expressions.\n
 • Use logic-state reasoning to predict digital outputs.\n• Recognize
  memory\, buses\, ports\, and basic digital-system blocks.\n• Verify d
 igital behavior using truth tables\, simulation\, or measured logic sign
 als.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are inten
 ded to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot explai
 n or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not count tha
 t item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use t
 he linked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nW
 EEK-END MASTERY RULE\nThis practical is the cumulative proof point for t
 he week. The week is Green only when the knowledge can be used on real h
 ardware/code/measurements without following a step-by-step tutorial.\n\n
