 o/alfred-university/week.html?week=13\n• Search this topic: https://nu
 mberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Schematics%20%2B%20T
 roubleshooting\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/a
 lfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Component-level anal
 og/digital troubleshooting and instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa
  Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; 
 use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 13 FOCUS: Schematics + 
 Block/Wiring Diagrams + Systematic Troubleshooting\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 6.1
 –6.10\; 8.× reinforcement\; 21.4/21.7 preview\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOS
 E: signal tracing\, test points\, pinouts\, datasheets\, expected-vs-act
 ual measurements\, reproduce→measure→isolate→verify.\n\nTHIS week'
 s resources:\n- PRIMARY — SparkFun How to Read a Schematic: https://le
 arn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/how-to-read-a-schematic/overview\n\nMASTERY G
 ATE: Trace power/signal flow on an unfamiliar diagram\, choose next test
  points\, locate a seeded fault\, and write a concise defect/root-cause 
 note.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts. Use learn ->retrieve
  -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> document. start each non
 -exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never use a missed 
 session as justification for an unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nS
 tudy only the resources tied to this week’s competencies. Create a one
 -page summary and 5–10 recall prompts. first 10 min: spaced retrieval 
 from older material.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Officia
 l Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive cop
 y and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. erra
 ta: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE
  — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.18 pp.159–164 + selected Ch.19
  pp.165–175 review + Appendix C pp.217–218.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.18 qu
 iz p.164 + Unit 8 review p.181.\nWHY: This is the book's strongest troub
 leshooting/diagram/test-point block and directly supports engineering-la
 b work.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook.
  Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever th
 e older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIR
 ED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 13)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be
  able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Read basic schematics\, block diag
 rams\, wiring diagrams\, pinouts\, connector tables\, and signal-flow dr
 awings.\n• Trace power and signals from source to destination and rela
 te schematic symbols to physical hardware.\n• Use datasheets to find p
 in functions\, ratings\, timing\, operating conditions\, and reference c
 ircuits.\n• Apply a systematic troubleshooting loop: verify symptom\, 
 gather evidence\, divide/isolate\, form hypothesis\, test\, repair\, ver
 ify.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are inten
 ded to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot explai
 n or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not count tha
 t item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use t
 he linked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nS
 IMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learnin
 g outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, writ
 e that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the nex
 t available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
