 \, ratings\, timing\, operating conditions\, and reference circuits.\n
 • Apply a systematic troubleshooting loop: verify symptom\, gather evi
 dence\, divide/isolate\, form hypothesis\, test\, repair\, verify.\n• 
 Use diagram/signal-path information to choose measurement points and iso
 late a fault.\n• Interpret expected values from a schematic before pro
 bing.\n• Use signal tracing\, substitution/known-good comparison\, con
 tinuity\, voltage\, and waveform checks appropriately.\n• Distinguish 
