SUMMARY:W16 • Prep — STM32 / ARM Development Kit
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN
  THESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.i
 o/alfred-university/week.html?week=16\n• Search this topic: https://nu
 mberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=STM32%20Setup%20%2B%
 20GPIO%20%2B%20SWD%20Debug\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2
 .github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: C + MCU 
 bring-up + serial buses + debug instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CET
 a Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\;
  use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nNeed by Week 16. Confirm ST
 M32 Nucleo or equivalent ARM/STM32-class board\, correct USB data cable\
 , STM32Cube IDE installation\, debugger access (on-board ST-LINK is fine
  when available)\, breadboard/jumpers\, and a known-good LED/button path
 .\n\n\nTODAY — ACTION CHECKLIST:\n1. Open LAB-016 in Practice → Lab 
 Center → Week 16.\n2. Virtual route: web browser plus the linked Wokwi
  STM32 simulator.\n3. Physical route: supported STM32 Nucleo/development
  board\; USB data cable (not charge-only)\; computer\; STM32Cube IDE/Cub
 eMX\; on-board ST-LINK or compatible SWD debugger\; breadboard\; jumper 
 wires\; LED and current-limiting resistor if the board's built-in LED is
  not used\; DMM\; oscilloscope optional.\n4. Confirm the board is recogn
 ized by the computer\, the correct board/debugger target is selected\, a
 nd all external signals use compatible logic voltage.\n5. If hardware or
  drivers are not ready\, use Wokwi so the scheduled work continues.\n\nR
 EFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Gui
 de\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page nu
 mbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/
 6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES\nB
 y the end of this event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\
 n• Know what equipment/parts are required for the next practical sessi
 on and what each item is for.\n• Confirm every critical item is ready\
 , compatible\, and safe to use before the lab begins.\n• Identify any 
 missing item early enough to obtain or substitute it without cancelling 
 the hands-on work.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks a
 bove are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still
  cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do
  not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up 
 list and use the linked official or supplemental resource before closing
  the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then che
 ck the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an 
 outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it 
 during the next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is requir
 ed.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Equipment\,Embedded\,CETa
END:VEVENT
