 al route: STM32/development board\; one documented I²C or SPI sensor br
 eakout\; USB data cable\; breadboard and jumper wires\; logic analyzer w
 ith leads\; device datasheet\; pull-up resistors if the breakout does no
 t include them.\n4. Confirm 3.3 V/5 V compatibility\, pinout\, ground\, 
 bus type\, I²C address or SPI chip-select wiring\, and analyzer input l
 imits before power.\n5. If the hardware combination is uncertain or inco
 mplete\, use the virtual route rather than guessing at connections.\n\nR
 EFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Gui
 de\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page nu
 mbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/
 6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES\nB
 y the end of this event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\
 n• Know what equipment/parts are required for the next practical sessi
 on and what each item is for.\n• Confirm every critical item is ready\
 , compatible\, and safe to use before the lab begins.\n• Identify any 
 missing item early enough to obtain or substitute it without cancelling 
 the hands-on work.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks a
 bove are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still
  cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do
  not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up 
 list and use the linked official or supplemental resource before closing
  the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then che
 ck the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an 
 outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it 
 during the next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is requir
 ed.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Equipment\,Embedded\,CETa
