DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN
  THESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.i
 o/alfred-university/week.html?week=17\n• Search this topic: https://nu
 mberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=UART%20%2B%20Python%
 20Serial\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-
 university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: C + MCU bring-up + serial 
 buses + debug instrumentation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career 
 Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive for
  repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 17 FOCUS: HOLIDAY LIGHT: UART + Python S
 erial + Computer Applications\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 16.1–16.10\; 12.1–12.
 4\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: UART framing/baud\, terminal use\, Python py
 Serial logging\, basic software/storage/backups/networking\; no New Year
 ’s Eve session.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- Serial Communication — 
 SparkFun: https://learn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/serial-communication/all\
 n-pySerial docs: https://pyserial.readthedocs.io/\n\nMASTERY GATE: Send/
 receive MCU serial data\, parse/log it in Python\, explain basic compute
 r/software/networking concepts\, and recover from a malformed response.\
 n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts. Use learn ->retrieve -> ca
 lculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> document. start each non-exam 
 study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never use a missed sessio
 n as justification for an unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nLearn T
 X/RX/GND\, framing/baud\, terminal use. Implement MCU status output.\n\n
 REFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Gu
 ide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page n
 umbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org
 /6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\
 nREAD / USE: Ch.16 pp.144–146 ports/interfaces + selected Ch.17 pp.149
 –155.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Short current-competency recall set\; book is ba
 ckground\, not the whole UART/Python skill.\nWHY: The 2016 book covers c
 omputer/port concepts but external UART and Python material is required 
 for current practical depth.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the p
 rimary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errat
 a control whenever the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nA
 FTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 17)\nBy the end of this 
 event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Explain UART 
 TX\, RX\, ground/reference\, baud rate\, frame format\, and asynchronous
  serial communication.\n• Send and receive UART data between an STM32 
 and a host computer.\n• Use a terminal/serial monitor to inspect traff
 ic and diagnose basic framing/configuration problems.\n• Use Python/py
 Serial to open a port\, configure timeout/baud\, send commands\, read re
 sponses\, and close cleanly.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources a
 nd tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If
  you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the se
 ssion\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short
  catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental resource befo
 re closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\
 , then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demon
 strate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list and 
 repair it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet logging
  is required.
