 c%20Analyzer%20%2B%20Sensors/Actuators\n• Engineering Library: https:/
 /numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTI
 ON: C + MCU bring-up + serial buses + debug instrumentation.\nRESOURCE P
 RIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required 
 work first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 18 FOCUS: 
 I2C/SPI + Logic Analyzer + Sensors/Actuators\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 12.5\; 13.
 5/13.7–13.12\; 8.10–8.12 reinforcement\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: One
  real I2C or SPI peripheral\, bus capture\, pull-ups/chip-select/clockin
 g\, sensor units\, PWM/output control.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- I2C 
 Tutorial — SparkFun: https://learn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/i2c/all\n- S
 PI Tutorial — SparkFun: https://learn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/serial-pe
 ripheral-interface-spi/all\n- Saleae support: https://support.saleae.com
 /\n\nMASTERY GATE: Implement one board-level bus\, capture and interpret
  transactions\, diagnose one bus fault\, and drive/read a real periphera
 l.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts. Use learn -> retrieve -
 >calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> document. Start each non-ex
 am study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never use a missed ses
 sion as justification for an unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nStud
 y only the resources tied to this week’s competencies. Create a one-pa
 ge summary and 5–10 recall prompts. first 10 min: spaced retrieval fro
 m older material.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official A
 ssociate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy a
 nd the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata:
  https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE 
 — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Use Ch.16/17 as reference only\; cur
 rent ETA competency wording + I2C/SPI tutorials control the interface le
 sson.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Unit 7 review pp.157–158 as cumulative digital r
 eview.\nWHY: I2C/SPI/modern interface expectations are not fully covered
  by this older book\, so current ETA + hands-on resources fill the gap.\
 nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current
  ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older 
 book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARN
 ING OUTCOMES (WEEK 18)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to
  explain or demonstrate:\n• Explain I2C controller/target roles\, SDA/
 SCL\, addressing\, pull-ups\, start/stop\, read/write\, ACK/NACK\, and b
 asic transactions.\n• Explain SPI controller/peripheral roles\, SCLK\,
  MOSI\, MISO\, chip select\, transaction framing\, and the idea of clock
  mode.\n• Choose I2C or SPI appropriately for a simple peripheral and 
 wire it correctly.\n• Use a logic analyzer to capture and decode UART 
 and the chosen I2C/SPI bus.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources an
 d tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If 
 you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the ses
 sion\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short 
 catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental resource befor
 e closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\,
  then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demons
 trate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list and r
 epair it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet logging 
 is required.
