DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN
  THESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.i
 o/alfred-university/week.html?week=18\n• Search this topic: https://nu
 mberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=I2C/SPI%20%2B%20Logi
 c%20Analyzer%20%2B%20Sensors/Actuators\n• Engineering Library: https:/
 /numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTI
 ON: C + MCU bring-up + serial buses + debug instrumentation.\nRESOURCE P
 RIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required 
 work first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 18 FOCUS: 
 I2C/SPI + Logic Analyzer + Sensors/Actuators\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 12.5\; 13.
 5/13.7–13.12\; 8.10–8.12 reinforcement\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: One
  real I2C or SPI peripheral\, bus capture\, pull-ups/chip-select/clockin
 g\, sensor units\, PWM/output control.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- I2C 
 Tutorial — SparkFun: https://learn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/i2c/all\n- S
 PI Tutorial — SparkFun: https://learn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/serial-pe
 ripheral-interface-spi/all\n- Saleae support: https://support.saleae.com
 /\n\nMASTERY GATE: Implement one board-level bus\, capture and interpret
  transactions\, diagnose one bus fault\, and drive/read a real periphera
 l.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts. Use learn -> retrieve -
 >calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> document. Start each non-ex
 am study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never use a missed ses
 sion as justification for an unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nAppl
 y the concept in LTspice\, C\, STM32\, schematic analysis or bench plann
 ing as appropriate. Predict results before simulation/code execution\; d
 eliberately create one fault when safe.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE 
 LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scann
 ed/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n
 • ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\n
 OFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Use Ch.16/17 as
  reference only\; current ETA competency wording + I2C/SPI tutorials con
 trol the interface lesson.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Unit 7 review pp.157–158 as
  cumulative digital review.\nWHY: I2C/SPI/modern interface expectations 
 are not fully covered by this older book\, so current ETA + hands-on res
 ources fill the gap.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary C
 ETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata contro
 l whenever the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TOD
 AY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 18)\nBy the end of this event\, 
 you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Choose I2C or SPI app
 ropriately for a simple peripheral and wire it correctly.\n• Use a log
 ic analyzer to capture and decode UART and the chosen I2C/SPI bus.\n• 
 Integrate a real sensor/peripheral and convert raw data into meaningful 
 units.\n• Interface a digital input/output or actuator safely and veri
 fy the end-to-end signal path.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources
  and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. 
 If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the 
 session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a sho
 rt catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental resource be
 fore closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned wor
 k\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or dem
 onstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list an
 d repair it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet loggi
 ng is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
