DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN
  THESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Assessment / readiness center: https://nu
 mberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/assessments.html\n• Progress Por
 tal: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/progress.html\n• 
 Search Everything: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/searc
 h.html\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-un
 iversity/resources.html\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core 
 → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive for repa
 ir or extra depth.\n\nBefore Spring coursework becomes heavy\, enter you
 r actual GSU Perimeter class/lab times\, commute\, known exam windows\, 
 and weekly homework load. Compare them to January-April study blocks. Sc
 hool wins conflicts. If the real class schedule materially changes avail
 ability\, revise the V5 calendar instead of trying to make up missed stu
 dy with marathons.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official 
 Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy 
 and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata
 : https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIR
 ED LEARNING OUTCOMES\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to e
 xplain or demonstrate:\n• Know the reduced study cadence once college 
 classes begin.\n• Understand that school exam weeks take priority and 
 missed self-study is rescheduled rather than crammed.\n• Know which co
 urse milestones must remain protected even when the weekly schedule flex
 es.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are intend
 ed to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain
  or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not count that
  item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use th
 e linked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSI
 MPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learning
  outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write
  that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next
  available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
