SUMMARY:W18 • Practical Gate — I²C/SPI + Logic Analyzer
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN
  THESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.i
 o/alfred-university/week.html?week=18\n• Search this topic: https://nu
 mberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=I2C/SPI%20%2B%20Logi
 c%20Analyzer%20%2B%20Sensors/Actuators\n• Lab Center: https://numbercl
 aw2.github.io/alfred-university/labs.html\n• Assessment Center: https:
 //numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/assessments.html\n• Engineer
 ing Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.h
 tml\nCAREER CONNECTION: C + MCU bring-up + serial buses + debug instrume
 ntation.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Co
 mplete the required work first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth
 .\n\nWEEK 18 FOCUS: I2C/SPI + Logic Analyzer + Sensors/Actuators\nETA/CE
 Ta SCOPE: 12.5\; 13.5/13.7–13.12\; 8.10–8.12 reinforcement\nCAREER/E
 MBEDDED PURPOSE: One real I2C or SPI peripheral\, bus capture\, pull-ups
 /chip-select/clocking\, sensor units\, PWM/output control.\n\nTHIS WEEK'
 S RESOURCES:\n- I2C Tutorial — SparkFun: https://learn.sparkfun.com/tu
 torials/i2c/all\n- SPI Tutorial — SparkFun: https://learn.sparkfun.com
 /tutorials/serial-peripheral-interface-spi/all\n- Saleae support: https:
 //support.saleae.com/\n\nMASTERY GATE: Implement one board-level bus\, c
 apture and interpret transactions\, diagnose one bus fault\, and drive/r
 ead a real peripheral.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts. Use
  learn -> retrieve ->calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> documen
 t. Start each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Ne
 ver use a missed session as justification for an unhealthy make-up marat
 hon.\n\nTODAY — ACTION CHECKLIST:\n1. Open LAB-018 — I²C / SPI Sens
 or + Logic Analyzer in Practice → Lab Center → Week 18.\n2. Choose o
 ne route. Virtual needs: Web browser only. Physical needs: STM32 board\,
  I²C/SPI sensor\, logic analyzer\, datasheet.\n3. Follow every numbered
  step under the route you selected\; predict the result before simulatin
 g\, building\, or measuring.\n4. Save the required evidence: Virtual wir
 ing diagram + code + decoded analyzer capture + data table + error case.
 \n5. Mark only the route you actually completed. A virtual completion do
 es not claim physical bench experience.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE 
 LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scann
 ed/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n
 • ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\n
 OFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Use Ch.16/17 as
  reference only\; current ETA competency wording + I2C/SPI tutorials con
 trol the interface lesson.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Unit 7 review pp.157–158 as
  cumulative digital review.\nWHY: I2C/SPI/modern interface expectations 
 are not fully covered by this older book\, so current ETA + hands-on res
 ources fill the gap.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary C
 ETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata contro
 l whenever the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TOD
 AY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 18)\nBy the end of this event\, 
 you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Explain I2C controlle
 r/target roles\, SDA/SCL\, addressing\, pull-ups\, start/stop\, read/wri
 te\, ACK/NACK\, and basic transactions.\n• Explain SPI controller/peri
 pheral roles\, SCLK\, MOSI\, MISO\, chip select\, transaction framing\, 
 and the idea of clock mode.\n• Choose I2C or SPI appropriately for a s
 imple peripheral and wire it correctly.\n• Use a logic analyzer to cap
 ture and decode UART and the chosen I2C/SPI bus.\n• Integrate a real s
 ensor/peripheral and convert raw data into meaningful units.\n• Interf
 ace a digital input/output or actuator safely and verify the end-to-end 
 signal path.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above a
 re intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still canno
 t explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not c
 ount that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list a
 nd use the linked official or supplemental resource before closing the g
 ap.\n\nWEEK-END MASTERY RULE\nThis practical is the cumulative proof poi
 nt for the week. The week is Green only when the knowledge can be used o
 n real hardware/code/measurements without following a step-by-step tutor
 ial.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check th
 e learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outco
 me\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it durin
 g the next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
