 rsity/search.html\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.i
 o/alfred-university/resources.html\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Car
 eer Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive
  for repair or extra depth.\n\nSearch current Atlanta-area permanent ful
 l-time hardware/test/R&D/electronics technician and engineering-aide rol
 es. Exclude construction/VDC/BIM/MEP roles. Log repeated skill requireme
 nts\, salary/schedule signals\, and gaps in the Career Proof sheet. Adju
 st only the role-specific add-on if the market shows a repeated requirem
 ent\; do not add random topics to the common core.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — 
 KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use
  your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASS
 IGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataShe
 et.pdf\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES\nBy the end of this
  event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Distinguish 
 R&D/engineering-lab\, hardware test/validation\, hardware integration\, 
 PCBA test\, and HIL-style bridge roles.\n• Recognize job-posting evide
 nce that indicates real electronics/hardware experience rather than inst
 allation/operations work.\n• Know which skill gaps are truly hard requ
 irements versus preferred qualifications and which role family best matc
 hes current readiness.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tas
 ks above are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you s
 till cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\
 , do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch
