SUMMARY:W19 • Learn — Cabling\, Audio/Video & Optical Systems
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN
  THESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.i
 o/alfred-university/week.html?week=19\n• Search this topic: https://nu
 mberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Cabling%20%2B%20Audi
 o/Video%20%2B%20Optical\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.gi
 thub.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Broad CETa 
 general-electronics coverage plus mixed-domain troubleshooting.\nRESOURC
 E PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the requir
 ed work first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 19 FOCU
 S: CETa-Specific Compression: Cabling + Audio/Video + Optical\nETA/CETa 
 SCOPE: 7.1–7.13\; 17.1–17.9\; 18.1–18.7\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: 
 Exam-focused depth for low-overlap material\; hands-on cable/connector r
 ecognition still supports technician roles.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n-
  Fiber Optic Lecture Series: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLC7C
 C6B17EF009849\n- BNC Connector on RG-58: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v
 =ktQVwfo-s9w\n- How Do Speakers Work?: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=j
 hg90zsjqt4\n- How Does an LCD Screen Work?: https://www.youtube.com/watc
 h?v=RZacFDPW_34\n\nMASTERY GATE: identify cable/display/audio/optical de
 vices\, choose termination/test methods\, explain likely fault symptoms\
 , and score ≥80% on the section quiz.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone 
 never counts. Use learn ->retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure ->
  debug -> document. start each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of 
 spaced recall. Never use a missed session as justification for an unheal
 thy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nFirst 10 min: spaced recall from prior 
 weeks. Study this week’s scoped material and make a one-page memory su
 mmary. Complete8–12 fresh CETa questions when ETA content applies. Sch
 ool work takes priority during exam-heavy weeks.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KE
 EP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use y
 our scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIG
 NMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet
 .pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Ch.14 p
 p.113–119 + Ch.21 pp.182–187 + Ch.9 optical-semiconductor section pp
 .76–77.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: Ch.14 quiz p.119 + Ch.21 quiz p.187.\nWHY: Use
 s the book for transmission/cabling and technician procedures\; current 
 ETA/video crosswalk fills fiber/audio-video gaps not covered as dedicate
 d chapters.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textb
 ook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control wheneve
 r the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — RE
 QUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 19)\nBy the end of this event\, you shoul
 d be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Recognize common cable\, conne
 ctor\, transmission-media\, audio/video\, and optical/fiber concepts in 
 the CETa scope.\n• Explain basic impedance\, shielding\, grounding\, c
 onnector integrity\, continuity\, and signal-loss concerns for cabling.\
 n• Describe basic audio/video signal paths and common failure points a
 t a technician level.\n• Explain basic optical/fiber concepts\, source
 /path/receiver thinking\, attenuation\, and handling cautions.\n\nCOVERA
 GE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are intended to cover e
 very item in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstra
 te one of these items after the session\, do not count that item as comp
 lete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use the linked offi
 cial or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETI
 ON RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learning outcomes bel
 ow. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one con
 cept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next available re
 view block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
