 0%2B%20Technician%20Procedures\n• Engineering Library: https://numberc
 law2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Broa
 d CETa general-electronics coverage plus mixed-domain troubleshooting.\n
 RESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the
  required work first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 
 20 FOCUS: CETa-Specific Compression: RF + Telecom + Technician Procedure
 s\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 19.1–19.11\; 20.1–20.5\; 21.1–21.9\nCAREER/EMBE
 DDED PURPOSE: Exam-focused RF/telecom plus documentation\, test planning
 \, parts research\, help-desk escalation and project discipline.\n\nTHIS
  WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- Basics of Antennas: https://www.youtube.com/watch?
 v=n8_iSL4xKj8\n- Introduction to Modulation: https://www.youtube.com/wat
 ch?v=mHvV_Tv8HDQ\n- Radio Fundamentals / LMR: https://www.youtube.com/wa
 tch?v=wuni9mHWjnE\n\nMASTERY GATE: explain propagation/modulation/SWR/wa
 velength/network basics and complete a technician-work scenario set with
  correct documentation and escalation choices.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching
  alone never counts. Use learn ->retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/mea
 sure -> debug -> document. start each non-exam study block with ~10 minu
 tes of spaced recall. Never use a missed session as justification for an
  unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nFirst 10 min: spaced recall from
  prior weeks. Study this week’s scoped material and make a one-page me
 mory summary. Complete8–12 fresh CETa questions when ETA content appli
 es. School work takes priority during exam-heavy weeks.\n\nREFERENCE HUB
  — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.
 : use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOO
 K ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErra
 taSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: 
 Ch.13 pp.104–112 + Ch.15 pp.120–130 + Ch.22 pp.188–193.\nQUIZ / RE
 VIEW: Ch.13 quiz p.112\, Ch.15 quiz p.130\, Unit 6 review p.131 and Ch.2
 2 quiz p.193.\nWHY: Compresses the low-embedded-priority RF/telecom mate
 rial while also learning the documentation behavior that matters in real
  technical jobs.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa 
 textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control wh
 enever the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY 
 — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 20)\nBy the end of this event\, you
  should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Explain introductory RF 
 concepts: frequency bands\, propagation\, modulation\, transmission line
 s\, antennas\, and standing-wave/impedance ideas at CETa level.\n• Rec
 ognize basic transmitter/receiver and telecom/telephone signal-path conc
 epts.\n• Understand technician procedures involving documentation\, re
 cords\, professionalism\, and technical communication.\n• Relate RF/te
 lecom symptoms to likely path\, connector\, configuration\, or signal pr
 oblems.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are in
 tended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot exp
 lain or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not count 
 that item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and us
 e the linked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n
 \nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the lear
 ning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, w
 rite that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the 
 next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
