SUMMARY:W24 • Project 1 Learn — Safe Hardware Bring-Up
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN
  THESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.i
 o/alfred-university/week.html?week=24\n• Search this topic: https://nu
 mberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Project%201%20Hardwa
 re%20Bring-Up\n• Lab Center: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-univ
 ersity/labs.html\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io
 /alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Portfolio-grade ha
 rdware/firmware/test evidence.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career 
 Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive for
  repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 24 FOCUS: Project 1 Hardware Bring-Up\nE
 TA/CETa SCOPE: Maintenance retrieval only\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Powe
 r\, GPIO\, button\, controlled output\, UART\, clean wiring\, rail measu
 rements/current draw.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- STM32 MCU Developer Z
 one: https://www.st.com/content/st_com/en/stm32-mcu-developer-zone.html\
 n- ETA Common Formulas: https://www.etai.org/Common_Formulas.pdf\n\nMAST
 ERY GATE: Boardpowers safely\, core I/O and UART work\, measurements are
  documented\, and at least one bring-up failure has a root-cause story.\
 n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts. Use learn -> retrieve ->ca
 lculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> document. Start each non-exam 
 study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never use a missed sessio
 n as justification for an unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nFirst 1
 0 min: spaced recall from prior weeks. Study this week’s scoped materi
 al and make a one-page memory summary. Complete8–12 fresh CETa questio
 ns when ETA content applies. School work takes priority during exam-heav
 y weeks.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate 
 CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PR
 INTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://
 www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK
  ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Reference Ch.11 pp.85–90\, Ch.18 pp.159–164
  and Ch.19 pp.165–175 during hardware bring-up.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: No new
  book quiz\; cite the relevant page in your troubleshooting notes when i
 t informs a decision.\nWHY: Reuses CETa material as real engineering-lab
  procedure instead of separating certification knowledge from job skill.
 \nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Curren
 t ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the older
  book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEAR
 NING OUTCOMES (WEEK 24)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able t
 o explain or demonstrate:\n• Perform safe first power-up using visual 
 inspection\, continuity checks\, a current-limited supply\, and measured
  power rails.\n• Verify board power\, ground\, reset/boot conditions\,
  GPIO\, and UART before adding complexity.\n• Measure voltage/current 
 and record baseline current draw.\n• Use SWD/UART diagnostics to separ
 ate hardware\, firmware\, and configuration faults.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nT
 he assigned resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item i
 n this outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of t
 hese items after the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write
  the concept on a short catch-up list and use the linked official or sup
 plemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFi
 nish the assigned work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you 
 cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a s
 hort catch-up list and repair it during the next available review block.
  No spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
