 o/alfred-university/week.html?week=24\n• Search this topic: https://nu
 mberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Project%201%20Hardwa
 re%20Bring-Up\n• Lab Center: https://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-univ
 ersity/labs.html\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.io
 /alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Portfolio-grade ha
 rdware/firmware/test evidence.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career 
 Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive for
  repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 24 FOCUS: Project 1 Hardware Bring-Up\nE
 TA/CETa SCOPE: Maintenance retrieval only\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Powe
 r\, GPIO\, button\, controlled output\, UART\, clean wiring\, rail measu
 rements/current draw.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- STM32 MCU Developer Z
 one: https://www.st.com/content/st_com/en/stm32-mcu-developer-zone.html\
 n- ETA Common Formulas: https://www.etai.org/Common_Formulas.pdf\n\nMAST
 ERY GATE: Boardpowers safely\, core I/O and UART work\, measurements are
  documented\, and at least one bring-up failure has a root-cause story.\
 n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts. Use learn -> retrieve ->ca
 lculate/code -> build/measure -> debug -> document. Start each non-exam 
 study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never use a missed sessio
 n as justification for an unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY — ACTIO
 N CHECKLIST:\n1. Review the Project 1 schematic\, pinout\, polarity\, su
 pply limits\, and current-limit plan before connecting power.\n2. Inspec
 t for shorts and wiring errors\; check resistance/continuity between pow
 er and ground with power off.\n3. Power one stage at a time and measure 
 each rail\, reset/boot state\, baseline current\, GPIO\, and UART/SWD ac
 cess.\n4. Introduce or capture one real fault\, isolate whether it is po
 wer\, wiring\, configuration\, firmware\, or measurement setup\, then ve
 rify the fix.\n5. Save the schematic/pinout\, pre-power checklist\, meas
 ured table\, current draw\, diagnostic capture\, and fault/fix note in P
 roject 1.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate
  CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the P
 RINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https:/
 /www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOO
 K ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Reference Ch.11 pp.85–90\, Ch.18 pp.159–16
 4 and Ch.19 pp.165–175 during hardware bring-up.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: No ne
 w book quiz\; cite the relevant page in your troubleshooting notes when 
 it informs a decision.\nWHY: Reuses CETa material as real engineering-la
 b procedure instead of separating certification knowledge from job skill
 .\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Curre
 nt ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the olde
 r book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEA
 RNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 24)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able 
 to explain or demonstrate:\n• Perform safe first power-up using visual
  inspection\, continuity checks\, a current-limited supply\, and measure
 d power rails.\n• Verify board power\, ground\, reset/boot conditions\
 , GPIO\, and UART before adding complexity.\n• Measure voltage/current
  and record baseline current draw.\n• Use SWD/UART diagnostics to sepa
 rate hardware\, firmware\, and configuration faults.\n• Apply staged b
 ring-up rather than powering everything at once.\n• Document bring-up 
 evidence and any fault/recovery story.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned r
 esources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outcom
 e list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items af
 ter the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept 
 on a short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental res
 ource before closing the gap.\n\nWEEK-END MASTERY RULE\nThis practical i
 s the cumulative proof point for the week. The week is Green only when t
 he knowledge can be used on real hardware/code/measurements without foll
 owing a step-by-step tutorial.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the ass
 igned work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot expla
 in or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-u
 p list and repair it during the next available review block. No spreadsh
 eet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
