SUMMARY:W25 • Project 1 Learn — Sensor & Interface Integration
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN
  THESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.i
 o/alfred-university/week.html?week=25\n• Search this topic: https://nu
 mberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Project%201%20Sensor
 %20/%20Interface%20Integration\n• Lab Center: https://numberclaw2.gith
 ub.io/alfred-university/labs.html\n• Engineering Library: https://numb
 erclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: P
 ortfolio-grade hardware/firmware/test evidence.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa
  Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; 
 use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 25 FOCUS: Project 1 Sen
 sor / Interface Integration\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 12.5/13.x/8.x spaced review
 \nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Integrate I2C/SPI sensor\, convert raw data t
 o engineering units\, capture bus traffic and handle disconnect/address 
 faults.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- I2C Tutorial —SparkFun: https://l
 earn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/i2c/all\n- SPI Tutorial —SparkFun: https:/
 /learn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/serial-peripheral-interface-spi/all\n- Sal
 eae support: https://support.saleae.com/\n\nMASTERY GATE: Sensor/interfa
 ce works end-to-end\, analyzer capture is interpretable\, and one physic
 al or protocol fault is diagnosed and documented.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watch
 ing alone never counts. Use learn ->retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/
 measure -> debug -> document. start each non-exam study block with ~10 m
 inutes of spaced recall. Never use a missed session as justification for
  an unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nFirst 10 min: spaced recall f
 rom prior weeks. Study this week’s scoped material and make a one-page
  memory summary. Complete8–12 fresh CETa questions when ETA content ap
 plies. School work takes priority during exam-heavy weeks.\n\nREFERENCE 
 HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th 
 ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in 
 BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTE
 rrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / US
 E: Reference Ch.16 pp.144–147 and Ch.17 pp.149–155\; use current ETA
  + datasheets/tutorials for the actual I2C/SPI device.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: N
 o new book quiz.\nWHY: Book architecture supports the concept\, while th
 e project proves modern interface implementation.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-
 edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wordin
 g + current ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or omits 
 a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 25)
 \nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrat
 e:\n• Integrate the chosen I2C/SPI sensor or peripheral into Project 1
 .\n• Read raw registers/data and convert values into meaningful engine
 ering units.\n• Verify bus activity with a logic analyzer and correlat
 e decoded traffic with firmware behavior.\n• Handle missing device\, w
 rong address/configuration\, timeout\, or invalid-data conditions.\n\nCO
 VERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are intended to cov
 er every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demon
 strate one of these items after the session\, do not count that item as 
 complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use the linked 
 official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMP
 LETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learning outcomes
  below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one
  concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next availabl
 e review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
