 o/alfred-university/week.html?week=25\n• Search this topic: https://nu
 mberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Project%201%20Sensor
 %20/%20Interface%20Integration\n• Lab Center: https://numberclaw2.gith
 ub.io/alfred-university/labs.html\n• Engineering Library: https://numb
 erclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: P
 ortfolio-grade hardware/firmware/test evidence.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa
  Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; 
 use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 25 FOCUS: Project 1 Sen
 sor / Interface Integration\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 12.5/13.x/8.x spaced review
 \nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Integrate I2C/SPI sensor\, convert raw data t
 o engineering units\, capture bus traffic and handle disconnect/address 
 faults.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- I2C Tutorial —SparkFun: https://l
 earn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/i2c/all\n- SPI Tutorial —SparkFun: https:/
 /learn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/serial-peripheral-interface-spi/all\n- Sal
 eae support: https://support.saleae.com/\n\nMASTERY GATE: Sensor/interfa
 ce works end-to-end\, analyzer capture is interpretable\, and one physic
 al or protocol fault is diagnosed and documented.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watch
 ing alone never counts. Use learn ->retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/
 measure -> debug -> document. start each non-exam study block with ~10 m
 inutes of spaced recall. Never use a missed session as justification for
  an unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nApply the topic in code\, sim
 ulation\, schematic analysis or troubleshooting. Predict expected behavi
 or before running/measuring. Record one failure or misconception and its
  correction.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associ
 ate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and th
 e PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: http
 s://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 
 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Reference Ch.16 pp.144–147 and Ch.17 pp.1
 49–155\; use current ETA + datasheets/tutorials for the actual I2C/SPI
  device.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: No new book quiz.\nWHY: Book architecture suppo
 rts the concept\, while the project proves modern interface implementati
 on.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Cur
 rent ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the ol
 der book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED L
 EARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 25)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be abl
 e to explain or demonstrate:\n• Verify bus activity with a logic analy
 zer and correlate decoded traffic with firmware behavior.\n• Handle mi
 ssing device\, wrong address/configuration\, timeout\, or invalid-data c
 onditions.\n• Confirm electrical interface requirements from the datas
 heet.\n• Document a working end-to-end peripheral path from hardware t
 hrough firmware to observed output.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned reso
 urces and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outcome l
 ist. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after
  the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on 
 a short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental resour
 ce before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigne
 d work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain o
 r demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up li
 st and repair it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet 
 logging is required.
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
