SUMMARY:W25 • Project 1 Lab — Verify Sensor / Interface Operation
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN
  THESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.i
 o/alfred-university/week.html?week=25\n• Search this topic: https://nu
 mberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Project%201%20Sensor
 %20/%20Interface%20Integration\n• Lab Center: https://numberclaw2.gith
 ub.io/alfred-university/labs.html\n• Engineering Library: https://numb
 erclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: P
 ortfolio-grade hardware/firmware/test evidence.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa
  Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; 
 use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 25 FOCUS: Project 1 Sen
 sor / Interface Integration\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 12.5/13.x/8.x spaced review
 \nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Integrate I2C/SPI sensor\, convert raw data t
 o engineering units\, capture bus traffic and handle disconnect/address 
 faults.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- I2C Tutorial —SparkFun: https://l
 earn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/i2c/all\n- SPI Tutorial —SparkFun: https:/
 /learn.sparkfun.com/tutorials/serial-peripheral-interface-spi/all\n- Sal
 eae support: https://support.saleae.com/\n\nMASTERY GATE: Sensor/interfa
 ce works end-to-end\, analyzer capture is interpretable\, and one physic
 al or protocol fault is diagnosed and documented.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watch
 ing alone never counts. Use learn ->retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/
 measure -> debug -> document. start each non-exam study block with ~10 m
 inutes of spaced recall. Never use a missed session as justification for
  an unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY — ACTION CHECKLIST:\n1. Verif
 y the sensor/peripheral datasheet pinout\, supply voltage\, logic levels
 \, bus address/mode\, and required pull-ups before wiring.\n2. Connect p
 ower\, ground\, and one interface at a time\; confirm the device respond
 s before adding application behavior.\n3. Read raw registers/data\, conv
 ert them to engineering units\, and compare the result with an expected 
 or reference condition.\n4. Capture I²C/SPI or serial evidence and test
  one failure case such as wrong address\, disconnected device\, timeout\
 , or invalid response.\n5. Save the wiring/interface diagram\, configura
 tion\, capture/log\, expected-versus-actual result\, and fault recovery 
 in Project 1.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Assoc
 iate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and t
 he PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: htt
 ps://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6
  BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Reference Ch.16 pp.144–147 and Ch.17 pp.
 149–155\; use current ETA + datasheets/tutorials for the actual I2C/SP
 I device.\nQUIZ / REVIEW: No new book quiz.\nWHY: Book architecture supp
 orts the concept\, while the project proves modern interface implementat
 ion.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Cu
 rrent ETA competency wording + current ETA errata control whenever the o
 lder book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED 
 LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 25)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be ab
 le to explain or demonstrate:\n• Integrate the chosen I2C/SPI sensor o
 r peripheral into Project 1.\n• Read raw registers/data and convert va
 lues into meaningful engineering units.\n• Verify bus activity with a 
 logic analyzer and correlate decoded traffic with firmware behavior.\n
 • Handle missing device\, wrong address/configuration\, timeout\, or i
 nvalid-data conditions.\n• Confirm electrical interface requirements f
 rom the datasheet.\n• Document a working end-to-end peripheral path fr
 om hardware through firmware to observed output.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe 
 assigned resources and tasks above are intended to cover every item in t
 his outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of thes
 e items after the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write th
 e concept on a short catch-up list and use the linked official or supple
 mental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinis
 h the assigned work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you can
 not explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a shor
 t catch-up list and repair it during the next available review block. No
  spreadsheet logging is required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
