SUMMARY:W26 • Project 1 Learn — Firmware Architecture
DESCRIPTION:ALFRED UNIVERSITY | AU-ESET 301\n\nALFRED STUDY PATH — OPEN
  THESE WHEN YOU NEED THEM\n• Week module: https://numberclaw2.github.i
 o/alfred-university/week.html?week=26\n• Search this topic: https://nu
 mberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Project%201%20Firmwa
 re%20Architecture\n• Engineering Library: https://numberclaw2.github.i
 o/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION: Portfolio-grade h
 ardware/firmware/test evidence.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: CETa Core → Career
  Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first\; use Deep Dive fo
 r repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 26 FOCUS: Project 1 Firmware Architectu
 re\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 13.10–13.12 spaced review\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE
 : Timers\, interrupts\, PWM\, nonblocking FSM\, timeouts\, error codes a
 nd diagnostic output.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- STM32 MCU Developer Z
 one: https://www.st.com/content/st_com/en/stm32-mcu-developer-zone.html\
 n\nMASTERY GATE: Firmware runs without long blocking delays\, timing is 
 measured\, error paths are exercised\, and architecture can be explained
  at interview depth.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts. Use l
 earn -> retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug ->document.
  Start each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Neve
 r use a missed session as justification for an unhealthy make-up maratho
 n.\n\nTODAY:\nFirst 10 min: spaced recall from priorweeks. Study this we
 ek’s scoped material and make a one-page memory summary. Complete 8–
 12 fresh CETa questions when ETA content applies. School work takes prio
 rity during exam-heavy weeks.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n
 • Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Googl
 e Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6
 th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL 
 STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Reference Ch.17 pp.151
 –155 and Ch.16 logic/sequential sections pp.136–143.\nQUIZ / REVIEW:
  Explain your firmware state machine and hardware-control flow without t
 he book open.\nWHY: Connects book control/programming concepts to struct
 ured embedded firmware.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the primar
 y CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata con
 trol whenever the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER 
 TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 26)\nBy the end of this event
 \, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Organize Project 1
  firmware into understandable modules with clear responsibilities.\n• 
 Use a nonblocking finite-state machine for system behavior.\n• Use tim
 ers/interrupts where appropriate without creating timing-dependent chaos
 .\n• Implement timeouts\, error states\, diagnostic messages\, and rec
 overable fault handling.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and t
 asks above are intended to cover every item in this outcome list. If you
  still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after the sessio
 n\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a short cat
 ch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental resource before c
 losing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, th
 en check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstra
 te an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up list and repa
 ir it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet logging is 
 required.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:Embedded\,CETa
