 RITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required wor
 k first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 28 FOCUS: Fau
 lt Injection + Troubleshooting + Test Report\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 6.x/8.x/21
 .4/21.7 spaced review\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Seed sensor disconnect\,
  wrong address\, bad wire\, timeout\, config error\, power fault and fir
 mware defect\; use one-change-at-a-time diagnosis.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOUR
 CES:\n- ETA CETa competencies: https://www.etai.org/comps/CETa_comps.pdf
 \n\nMASTERY GATE: At least three interview-ready failure stories\, inclu
 ding onephysical/electrical fault\, each with reproducible→measure→i
 solate→fix→verify evidence.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: watching alone never co
 unts. Use learn -> retrieve -> calculate/code ->build/measure -> debug -
 > document. Start each non-exam study block with~10 minutes of spaced re
 call. Never use a missed session as justification for an unhealthy make-
 up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nFirst 10 min: spaced recall from prior weeks. St
 udy this week’s scoped material and make a one-page memory summary. Co
 mplete 8–12 fresh CETa questions when ETA content applies. School work
  takes priority during exam-heavy weeks.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE
  LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scan
 ned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n
 • ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\n
 OFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Reference Ch.18
  pp.159–164 + Ch.22 pp.188–193 + Appendix C pp.217–218.\nQUIZ / RE
 VIEW: Use troubleshooting/technical-writing questions as retrieval\; foc
 us on evidence quality.\nWHY: Fault injection and test reports are where
  CETa troubleshooting turns into employer-ready proof.\nSOURCE RULE: The
  6th-edition book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency w
 ording + current ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or o
 mits a current topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEE
 K 28)\nBy the end of this event\, you should be able to explain or demon
 strate:\n• Design and execute deliberate fault-injection tests.\n• U
 se the troubleshooting sequence: reproduce\, measure\, isolate\, hypothe
 size\, test\, fix\, and verify.\n• Distinguish hardware\, firmware\, i
 nterface\, test-fixture\, power\, and host-script faults.\n• Collect D
 MM/scope/logic-analyzer/log evidence that supports root cause.\n\nCOVERA
 GE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are intended to cover e
 very item in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain or demonstra
 te one of these items after the session\, do not count that item as comp
 lete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use the linked offi
 cial or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETI
 ON RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learning outcomes bel
 ow. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write that one con
 cept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next available re
 view block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
