 OURCES:\n- ETA CETa competencies: https://www.etai.org/comps/CETa_comps.
 pdf\n\nMASTERY GATE: At least three interview-ready failure stories\, in
 cluding onephysical/electrical fault\, each with reproducible→measure
 →isolate→fix→verify evidence.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: watching alone neve
 r counts. Use learn -> retrieve -> calculate/code ->build/measure -> deb
 ug -> document. Start each non-exam study block with~10 minutes of space
 d recall. Never use a missed session as justification for an unhealthy m
 ake-up marathon.\n\nTODAY — ACTION CHECKLIST:\n1. Write at least three
  deliberate faults before testing: one hardware/power/wiring fault\, one
  firmware/configuration fault\, and one interface/test-fixture fault.\n2
 . For each fault\, record the expected symptom\, reproduce it safely\, a
 nd collect DMM/scope/logic/serial evidence.\n3. Follow reproduce → mea
 sure → isolate → hypothesize → test → fix → retest\; do not ch
 ange multiple variables at once.\n4. Run the original passing test again
  after each repair to check for regression.\n5. Save a technical report 
 containing test setup\, fault matrix\, observations\, root cause\, corre
 ctive action\, and final PASS/FAIL evidence.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP T
 HESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your 
