 mberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/search.html?q=Instrumentation%20%2
 B%20Solder/Rework/Harness%20Role%20Proof\n• Lab Center: https://number
 claw2.github.io/alfred-university/labs.html\n• Engineering Library: ht
 tps://numberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CON
 NECTION: Portfolio-grade hardware/firmware/test evidence.\nRESOURCE PRIO
 RITY: CETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required wor
 k first\; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 29 FOCUS: Ins
 trumentation + Solder/Rework/Harness Role Proof\nETA/CETa SCOPE: 5.x/7.x
 /8.x spaced review\nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Scope/DMM/logic captures\, 
 clean rework\, wire termination/simple harness\, continuity verification
 \, power-up checklist and engineering photos.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\
 n- Soldering Tutorial Part 1: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J5Sb21qbpE
 Q\n- BNC Connector on RG-58: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ktQVwfo-s9w
 \n\nMASTERY GATE: Create a concise engineering dossier showing prototype
 →bring-up→fault→measurements→repair/rework→retest with profess
 ional evidence.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: Watching alone never counts. Use learn 
 -> retrieve -> calculate/code -> build/measure -> debug ->document. Star
 t each non-exam study block with ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never use
  a missed session as justification for an unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\
 nTODAY — ACTION CHECKLIST:\n1. Choose one honest physical role-proof t
 ask: controlled solder/rework\, a small labeled wire harness\, or an ins
 trumented prototype repair. Use a virtual/documentation route only for t
 he analytical portions\; physical workmanship claims require real work.\
 n2. Record the original condition\, pinout/schematic\, safety/ESD plan\,
  tools/materials\, and acceptance criteria.\n3. Perform the work\, then 
 inspect it and verify continuity\, polarity\, strain relief\, insulation
 \, and absence of shorts before power.\n4. Power and test safely with DM
 M plus the most relevant scope\, logic-analyzer\, debugger\, or serial e
 vidence.\n5. Save clear before/after photos\, measurements\, fault/repai
 r story\, retest result\, and a short explanation another technician cou
 ld follow.\n\nREFERENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associat
 e CET Study Guide\, 6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the 
 PRINTED page numbers in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https:
 //www.etai.org/6thEdASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BO
 OK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD / USE: Reference Ch.19 pp.165–175 + Ch.20 pp.176
 –180 + Ch.14 transmission-line/cabling sections pp.115–118.\nQUIZ / 
 REVIEW: No new book quiz\; demonstrate the skills physically.\nWHY: This
  week is about instruments\, rework and harness/cabling proof\, so the b
 ook serves as a procedure/reference source.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-editio
 n book is the primary CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + cu
 rrent ETA errata control whenever the older book differs or omits a curr
 ent topic.\n\nAFTER TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 29)\nBy t
 he end of this event\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n
 • Use DMM\, oscilloscope\, logic analyzer\, bench supply\, and debugge
 r evidence confidently in one coherent hardware story.\n• Demonstrate 
 clean soldering/rework\, wire termination\, continuity verification\, an
 d simple harness/prototype workmanship.\n• Perform a controlled protot
 ype repair or rework and verify the result.\n• Create an R&D/engineeri
 ng-lab role-proof dossier: prototype\, bring-up\, problem\, measurements
 \, repair\, retest.\n• Explain workmanship/ESD/safety decisions profes
 sionally.\n• Show that the physical build is understandable and servic
 eable by another technical person.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resou
 rces and tasks above are intended to cover every item in this outcome li
 st. If you still cannot explain or demonstrate one of these items after 
 the session\, do not count that item as complete. Write the concept on a
  short catch-up list and use the linked official or supplemental resourc
 e before closing the gap.\n\nSIMPLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned
  work\, then check the learning outcomes below. If you cannot explain or
  demonstrate an outcome\, write that one concept on a short catch-up lis
 t and repair it during the next available review block. No spreadsheet l
 ogging is required.
END:VALARM
