 sume%20%2B%20Interview%20Green-Light\n• Engineering Library: https://n
 umberclaw2.github.io/alfred-university/resources.html\nCAREER CONNECTION
 : Portfolio-grade hardware/firmware/test evidence.\nRESOURCE PRIORITY: C
 ETa Core → Career Core → Deep Dive. Complete the required work first
 \; use Deep Dive for repair or extra depth.\n\nWEEK 30 FOCUS: Portfolio 
 + Resume + Interview Green-Light\nETA/CETa SCOPE: CETa maintenance only\
 nCAREER/EMBEDDED PURPOSE: Finish README/block diagram/schematic/photos/t
 est evidence\; targeted Hardware/R&D and Test/Validation resume\; 5+ sto
 ries\; readiness scorecard.\n\nTHIS WEEK'S RESOURCES:\n- GitHub Skills 
 — Introduction to GitHub: https://github.com/skills/introduction-to-gi
 thub\n\nMASTERY GATE: Common core + Project 1 + one role add-on demonstr
 able\; portfolio and resume-defensible\; 90-sec transition story\, 2-min
  project overview and 5-min technical deep dive ready.\n\nSYSTEM RULES: 
 Watching alone never counts. Use learn -> retrieve -> calculate/code -> 
 build/measure -> debug ->document. Start each non-exam study block with 
 ~10 minutes of spaced recall. Never use a missed session as justificatio
 n for an unhealthy make-up marathon.\n\nTODAY:\nFirst 10 min: spaced rec
 all from priorweeks. Study this week’s scoped material and make a one-
 page memory summary. Complete 8–12 fresh CETa questions when ETA conte
 nt applies. School work takes priority during exam-heavy weeks.\n\nREFER
 ENCE HUB — KEEP THESE LINKS:\n• Official Associate CET Study Guide\,
  6th ed.: use your scanned/Google Drive copy and the PRINTED page number
 s in BOOK ASSIGNMENT.\n• ETA 6th-ed. errata: https://www.etai.org/6thE
 dASTErrataSheet.pdf\n\nOFFICIAL STUDY GUIDE — V6 BOOK ASSIGNMENT\nREAD
  / USE: Reference Ch.21 pp.182–187 + Ch.22 pp.188–193.\nQUIZ / REVIE
 W: No exam-style quiz\; convert these chapters into polished resume bull
 ets\, portfolio captions and interview stories.\nWHY: The book's technic
 ian professionalism and technical-writing material directly strengthens 
 the application package.\nSOURCE RULE: The 6th-edition book is the prima
 ry CETa textbook. Current ETA competency wording + current ETA errata co
 ntrol whenever the older book differs or omits a current topic.\n\nAFTER
  TODAY — REQUIRED LEARNING OUTCOMES (WEEK 30)\nBy the end of this even
 t\, you should be able to explain or demonstrate:\n• Present Project 1
  as an employer-facing engineering artifact rather than a hobby build.\n
 • Write truthful\, role-specific resume bullets for R&D electronics\, 
 hardware test/validation\, and integration roles.\n• Organize GitHub/p
 ortfolio evidence so a reviewer can understand the problem\, design\, me
 asurements\, failures\, and results quickly.\n• Deliver a clear 90-sec
 ond career-transition story and a 2-minute/5-minute Project 1 explanatio
 n.\n\nCOVERAGE AUDIT\nThe assigned resources and tasks above are intende
 d to cover every item in this outcome list. If you still cannot explain 
 or demonstrate one of these items after the session\, do not count that 
 item as complete. Write the concept on a short catch-up list and use the
  linked official or supplemental resource before closing the gap.\n\nSIM
 PLE COMPLETION RULE\nFinish the assigned work\, then check the learning 
 outcomes below. If you cannot explain or demonstrate an outcome\, write 
 that one concept on a short catch-up list and repair it during the next 
 available review block. No spreadsheet logging is required.
